# 0097-export-info-plist-first-zip64.patch -- the owner's field bug: a FULL export (South Park The Stick of Truth, multi-GB RomFS inside) signed with FlareStore (zsign-based) failed:
# "Signing failed: Can't get BundleID, BundleVersion, or BundleExecute in Info.plist!". Applies after 0096. UNTESTED ON DEVICE: compiled, its pure part ran in the host harness, and the
# ZIP64 layout was MEASURED with the export's own ZipArchive (probe97, below).
#
# CAUSE: GameAppExport.Plan added the app's Info.plist LAST, after extract/RomFS.img: its local header lay beyond 4 GiB (a ZIP64 offset; measured: byte 4,609,540,297 behind a 4.3 GiB
#   RomFS), and an unzip that mishandles ZIP64 gives no Info.plist to zsign's GetSignFolderInfo (it needs CFBundleIdentifier and CFBundleExecutable). Also: an Info.plist that could not
#   be read became an EMPTY dictionary (no CFBundleExecutable, no CFBundleVersion) instead of an error.
# FIX:
#   1. The entry order (ExportZip.Order): the app's Info.plist FIRST, the framework's second, the rest of the bundle (the executable, icons, PkgInfo, Frameworks/*) in its order, then the
#      game's data smaller than 64 MB (flat modules, profile, manifest, games/<id>, small shader files), then its big files by size, RomFS.img last: every piece of bundle metadata below 4 GiB.
#   2. Past 4 GB (the full IPA, or a light one with very large shaders): before the export, "This IPA is larger than 4 GB: some signing tools (FlareStore and other on-device signers) cannot
#      open it. Use the slim export (the game's files are copied beside it) if the install fails." with "Light IPA instead (…)" and "Export it anyway (…)"; the log says
#      "export: 14.6 GB, ZIP64 (entries above 4 GB: …RomFS.img)" (or ", no ZIP64").
#   3. After writing, before the .part becomes the .ipa (VerifyIpa): the .ipa opened again with ZipArchive, its Payload/<app>/Info.plist parsed, CFBundleIdentifier, CFBundleExecutable and
#      CFBundleVersion present, its local header offset read from the central directory (ExportZip.LocalHeaderOffset: ZIP64 records and extra fields) and below 4 GiB, logged
#      ("export: Info.plist checked: <id> · <exe> · <version>, at byte N (below 4 GB)"); else the export fails with what is wrong and the .part is removed.
#   4. The Info.plist is never written from an empty dictionary: an unreadable bundle Info.plist (InfoPlist, FrameworkPlist's app plist) throws "the app's own Info.plist could not be read (…)",
#      and a plist missing a required key is refused before writing.
#   The light (slim) export keeps the RomFS beside the .ipa; it is ordered and checked the same way, and warned about too if it passes 4 GB.
#
# VERIFIED (2026-11-22, M1 Pro): check-patches-apply.sh: every patch 0010-0097 applies in order, no fuzz, no offset; the repository's patches give exactly the compiled tree. Compile
#   (-t:Compile): 0 errors / 40 warnings, the same per file and code as before 0080. Host harness (harness97: … P94;P97): 368 of 368 checks (10 new: the order, ZIP64 before/after, the 4 GB
#   rule and its words, the required keys, the central directory read back, the wiring); 9 of 10 mutations killed by the harness, the 10th (the ZIP64 extra field's order) by probe97.
#   probe97 (System.IO.Compression's ZipArchive, ~8.6 GB written and removed): the old order puts Info.plist at byte 4,609,540,297; 0097's order at byte 0; an entry whose sizes and offset
#   are all ZIP64 is found at its local header (4,399,824,977).
# NOT VERIFIED: a real FlareStore / zsign install of the new .ipa; whether that signer's unzip also mishandles a ZIP64 RomFS entry (the warning offers the light export for that).
# NEW UI STRINGS: "A large IPA", ExportZip.Warning, "Light IPA instead (", "Export it anyway ("; log lines ", ZIP64 (entries above 4 GB: ", ", no ZIP64", "export: Info.plist checked: ",
#   " (below 4 GB)", "could not be read (".
